<title>SRI LANKA: Development up as demand outpaces supply.</title>
<headline>Development up as demand outpaces supply.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Development Finance Corporation of Ceylon Ltd rose 5.56 percent or 15 rupees to 285 on Thursday, as demand outpaced supply, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a supply and demand situation and the sharp rise is due to a lack of shares,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Development Finance is one of two blue chip development finance institutions listed in Colombo.</p>
<p>The share is the most capitalised stock trading in Colombo and has a big impact on the all share index, brokers said.</p>
<p>--- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
